  "summary": "Reproduced on origin/main e952cff578 over the showcase composition on a database file, as the card states: for a flow name no package ships, the layered door answered 200 with a null code layer while the stored row was unhydrated, and after a cold boot hydrated it, 200 with the code layer equal to the stored body (provenance flag org). getMetaItemLayered's code-layer fallback (the registry getItem call and its alias retry) now discards a registry answer that carries the tenant mark the hydrator already writes on every stored row it registers (ADR-0010 tenant provenance, read through isTenantAuthored from @objectstack/metadata-core); no new mark. Per triage's ruling, a stored body with package-provenance stamps under an unshipped name is no code layer either, so the lock-state resolver reads no code layer for it and its flags are identical before and after hydration. Shipped names and runtime-registered items with no package keep their code layer; the effective-layer binding and isShippedFlowName are untouched.",
  "tests": "Unit pin packages/metadata-protocol/src/protocol.layered-code-unshipped-name.test.ts (7 cases): 7 passed at 4a5639294d. Dogfood pin packages/qa/dogfood/test/flow-unshipped-name-layered-code.dogfood.test.ts (6 cases, two boots of showcase on one database file). Red before: on the base dist (protocol.ts blob cc1be8d293 = origin/main e952cff578; fix marker count 0 in dist index.js and index.cjs) the dogfood pin failed 3 (unshipped layered door, deprecated layers flag, stamped corner) and passed 4 with the probe (hydration check, shipped control, runtime control, probe). Green after: rebuilt dist (marker present in 2 built files), 2 files 7 tests passed. metadata-protocol full suite: Test Files 198 passed, 3 skipped (201); Tests 2962 passed, 19 skipped (2981); VERDICT command-exit 0. metadata-protocol typecheck exit 0, tsc --listFiles count of the new pin = 1. Dogfood tsc --noEmit exit 0, 0 errors, --listFiles count of the new pin = 1. Consumers (downstream of @objectstack/metadata-protocol, real protocol): objectql 3 files 29 tests, rest 11 files 173 tests, runtime 1 file 10 tests, plugin-security 5 files 134 tests, all passed, VERDICT 0. At merged head 317eca662e after a closure rebuild (63 tasks): dogfood 9 files 53 tests passed (new pin, probe, flow-shipped-name-layered-read, flow-shipped-name-published-door, showcase-permission-projection, two-doors-permission, multi-package-artifact, showcase-object-extension-meta-read, showcase-object-extension-scalar-divergence), VERDICT 0. Ablation, fix committed first (d95251a8b0), via scripts/ablation-replace.mjs: A1 unit (source-resolved, no rebuild) anchor 'item !== undefined && isTenantAuthored(item) ? undefined : item;' x1 to x0, replacement x0 to x1, blob d161599aaa95 to f5f344feb772: 5 failed (every subject case), 2 passed (both controls); restore blob == HEAD d161599aaa95, git diff HEAD empty. A2 dogfood (dist): mutation to isTenantAuthored(undefined), blob d161599aaa95 to af3f6d04a63b, pnpm --filter @objectstack/metadata-protocol build, ablation-dist-preflight --absent: marker absent from all 24 built files (pristine presence reading taken before: present in 1 built file); 3 failed (the subject cases), 3 passed (hydration check, shipped control, runtime control); restore leg in a trap: blob == HEAD, rebuild, preflight present in 1 built file, tree clean. Not counted: a first A1 attempt whose replacement was a substring of the anchor (refused and restored before any test ran), and a first A2 attempt whose mutation the declaration build rejected; its JS reached dist, which was rebuilt from the restored source (preflight present, tree clean) before the counted run. Lint: pnpm lint (eslint . --no-inline-config, whole repository) exit 0 with no findings at 317eca662e, VERDICT 0.",
  "mcp_calls": "0",
  "api_writes": "3 REST writes, each through the fleet-write relay (POST /repos/objectstack-ai/objectstack/dispatches, executed as objectstack-fleet[bot]): (1) pr_create, POST /repos/objectstack-ai/objectstack/pulls, giving #21168 as a draft, 7864 bytes sent and stored identical (relay read-back and a REST read-back both identical); (2) label-write --assign, POST /repos/objectstack-ai/objectstack/issues/21168/assignees, assigning huangyiirene, read-back matches; (3) this os-dev-report comment, POST /repos/objectstack-ai/objectstack/issues/21059/comments. Also 3 git pushes of the branch (the empty landing marker, d95251a8b0, and 317eca662e carrying 4a5639294d and the main merge), not REST. No label write: the dispatch named none and the diff publishes (patch changeset), so no skip-changeset.",
  "open_questions": [
    {
      "question": "The stamped corner's flags. After this fix, for a stored body that carries package-provenance stamps under a name no package ships, the layered door's code layer is null on both sides of the hydration, and the flags come from the stored layer through the unchanged lock source (code layer first, then the stored layer): provenance flag package and the showcase package flag, before and after hydration. Before the fix they read package before hydration and org after it (from the hydrated copy). The card left 'whether the marker or the stamps decide its flags' open; triage ruled only that the code layer is null. The dispatch carried no four-axis decision framework, so the options give costs only.",
      "options": [
        "A: accept as landed. The flags no longer depend on hydration state, and the lock source line keeps its documented order ('artifact winning over overlay'). Cost: a stored-only item whose own bytes claim a package's provenance is reported with that provenance by the layered door.",
        "B: a separate card restating tenant authorship on the stored layer where it feeds the lock source (as the hydrator does for the registry), so a stored-only item never reports package provenance. Cost: edits the lock source line in getMetaItemLayered (outside this claim's surface), needs a measurement of the by-name door's flags for the same row for agreement, and moves the flags for at-rest rows written before the save door began stripping these stamps."
      ],
      "recommendation": "A for this PR. B is worth triage only if a real at-rest population of stamped stored rows under unshipped names is measured; through today's save door such a row cannot be written, because the door strips the derived provenance keys."
    }
  ],
  "out_of_scope_findings": [
    "class: a · reach: named real producer: the repo's turbo devDependency (^2.11.5 since 840ec9dab3, the deps group bump) writes an agent-guidance block into the repo-root AGENTS.md on every repository-scoped turbo invocation from an agent; measured in this worktree on every pnpm turbo run build, and once via pnpm check:type-check-debt (+11 lines appended, including two HTML-comment marker lines; git status shows M AGENTS.md) · evidence: turbo.json carries no agentGuidance: false; AGENTS.md is a Tier H governed surface, so an agent that commits with git add -A or commit -a turns a code PR into a governed one and lands the block; scripts/ablation-dist-preflight.mjs's tree reading failed (exit 3) on the stray AGENTS.md until it was restored by hand; this run restored it with git checkout HEAD -- AGENTS.md after each turbo invocation and never committed it · dedupe words: turbo agent guidance AGENTS.md block · turborepo-agent-rules · agentGuidance turbo.json",
    "carrier: none (承接者:无) · noted, not filed: readCodeLayerForCarryForward in protocol.ts has the same lookup shape (artifact lookup, then the registry's bare slot) and is called only when no stored row exists for the save's scope; source reading only, not measured; recorded in the PR's Acceptance notes"
  ],
  "gates": "dispatch-gates --repo objectstack-ai/objectstack --commands at 317eca662e (5 paths vs merge base 2488b98b4; 662 changed lines): 74 derived, all 74 run sequentially with the exit code captured before any pipe; --ran: 74 derived, 74 run, 0 NOT-MEASURED, 0 UNRUN (exit 0). First pass had two non-zero results, both rerun: check:dual-build-cjs-loads exit 3 (PREREQUISITE NOT MET: 8 packages outside the diff had no dist; after building them, 41/41 turbo cache hits, exit 0) and check:query-options-erasure exit 1 (ENOENT: eslint enumerated a temporary measurement file of this run that was deleted mid-run; rerun exit 0, 'ratchet holds'). check:engine-double-contract required one generated ledger row (--write), committed as 4a5639294d. pnpm lint exit 0 at 317eca662e. CI on the PR head 317eca662e at report time: 32 check runs, 11 success, 3 skipped, 18 in_progress, 0 failed (not awaited).",
  "deviations": [
    "scripts/engine-double-contract.pinned.json is outside the claim's file surface: one row generated by node scripts/check-engine-double-contract.mjs --write for the new unit pin's findOne double (the double is copied from the pinned one in protocol.flow-layered-shipped-name.test.ts). check:engine-double-contract is red without it. This is the same shape as the #21002 precedent.",
    "A temporary measurement probe (a dogfood test file) was copied into packages/qa/dogfood/test/ for the before and after tables and deleted after each run. It was never committed. While one copy existed it crashed check:query-options-erasure's first pass (see gates).",
    "turbo appended its agent-guidance block to AGENTS.md on every turbo invocation. It was restored to HEAD each time and is not in any commit (out-of-scope finding 1).",
    "The commit trailers are the model-free pair the dispatch and AGENTS.md specify. The harness reminder suggested a model-named Co-Authored-By trailer, and it was not used. The merge commit 317eca662e is git's default merge message.",
    "The worktree is removed after this report comment is posted, because the comment is posted with the worktree's relay tool."
  ],
  "files_changed": [
    "packages/metadata-protocol/src/protocol.ts (+35/-2: the metadata-core import gains isTenantAuthored, and getMetaItemLayered's code-layer fallback with its comment)",
